  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only models dominate image-only, and the strongest result is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with validation accuracy 0.650 and F1 0.628, improving over PCA multiprofile avgpool. The key uncertainty is whether this gain is specific to scvi_n200 or whether another pretrained RNA encoder, scgpt, can match or exceed it under the same profile and aggregation. config_008 changes only the RNA encoder while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, directly isolating the representation choice. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest RNA-only direction, has plausible high immediate performance, and will clarify which RNA encoder should be used before testing more complex multimodal configurations."
}

